📥 Installation Guide
Because this is a custom developer tool, it must be loaded unpacked via your browser's developer interface:

Download the Repository: Click the green Code button at the top of this GitHub page and click Download ZIP.

Extract Files: Unzip the downloaded folder somewhere safe on your desktop. Ensure all 5 core files (manifest.json, popup.html, popup.js, banner.mp4, and AllowedUsersKIS) remain together in the same folder.

Open Extensions Page: Open Google Chrome, Brave, or Microsoft Edge, and navigate to:

chrome://extensions/

Enable Developer Mode: Toggle the Developer mode switch in the top-right corner to ON.

Load the Extension: Click the Load unpacked button in the top-left corner, select your extracted project folder, and click open.

Pin the Tool: Click the extension puzzle piece icon (🧩) next to your browser's search bar and click the pin icon next to KABIR DISCORD RULER to keep it accessible.

🎮 How To Use
Open Discord Web: Navigate to the Discord web client ([discord.com/app](https://discord.com/app)) in your browser and click into the specific text channel or DM where you want the script to interact.

Launch the Engine: Click the 👑 icon in your browser toolbar to draw the extension interface.

Cloud Authentication Verification:

The tool will automatically check your authorization against the cloud user registry (AllowedUsersKIS).

When prompted, type in your registered Discord username. If your name matches the allowed registry, the "Run Engine" button will instantly unlock.

Configure your Variables:

🎯 Subject Name: Enter a custom string. Any time you include [Subject] in your text fields, it will automatically be replaced with this name when sending.

💬 Messages: Type or paste your message list (one entry per line).

🎨 Text Art Mode: Turn this on if you are pasting complex multiline ASCII text art configurations. Surround your arts with textart{ and }textart boundaries so the script treats the block as a single cohesive block instead of splitting it line-by-line.

💥 Burst Mode: Turn this switch on if you want to push every single message in your current queue sequence into the channel instantly all at once.

⏱️ Message Delay: If Burst Mode is off, specify the custom rest delay (in seconds) the automation engine should wait before pasting the next sequential message.

Trigger Operations: Click Run Engine to begin execution. Click Stop at any point to completely halt text transmission.

⚠️ Important: The browser requires the Discord tab to stay active and selected for the automation macro scripts to inject keystroke inputs cleanly into the chat box container framework.
